
=== self-test: a clean synthetic run ===
run clean: 1280x720, 90.0 px a unit, residual window 9 px rows

A. Row seams. Each cell: rms % of the row residual, lowest, highest (luma), and the share of pixel rows at least 1 luma dark. One dark row is the picture's own (the background cell at a zero). A share of them is a lattice.
   vs tile: the row means' difference from the same subject's tile: rms, lowest, highest.
  z
    now              1.76%   -8.29   +2.04  21.1%   vs tile  3.125  -10.27   +0.00
    overlap          0.08%   -1.18   +0.84   0.2%   vs tile  0.161   -2.19   +0.32
    tile             0.08%   -1.57   +0.93   0.4%   vs tile  0.000   +0.00   +0.00
    flat_control     1.75%   -8.17   +2.22  21.5%
  tan
    now              1.76%   -6.30   +2.64  20.6%   vs tile  2.348   -7.80   +0.00
    overlap          0.35%   -1.66   +1.76   0.8%   vs tile  0.441   -2.98   +0.92
    tile             0.37%   -1.61   +1.71   2.2%   vs tile  0.000   +0.00   +0.00

B. The mirror against the frame, row residuals. r on the same rows, r one row off, and rms of frame and mirror. Pixels: rms of 255 over the plate.
  z         now    r +1.000 off1 -0.356  rms 2.671 / 2.670  pixels 0.29
  z         tile   r +0.997 off1 +0.056  rms 0.127 / 0.129  pixels 0.29
